{"kind":"assert","text":"Review note for Hugh: resolve a record's file references once, then use that result for both its prose and evidence list.\n\nThe four-reader rollout exposed a concrete source of confusion. In #21221, the current reader baseline link opens a missing repository file, while the listed attachment with the same name opens all 150 lines. The [record detail](ui/src/components/RecordDetail.tsx@b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c:78) sends prose to the renderer without attachment names, then loads the evidence list separately. The [renderer](ui/src/components/Preview.tsx@b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c:15) already supports the distinction when given those names. I reproduced the two API results independently; Codex recorded the actual browser clicks in #21229.\n\nThe small, high-impact remedy is one bounded metadata lookup per displayed record, shared by all its references. An attachment mention should behave like its evidence-list link; a source file should remain reachable when the names collide. This removes a navigation trap and repeated author explanations without adding another filing or approval step. I filed #21231 for implementation after the current deployment-doc correction, including collision, record-switching, security and actual-browser checks. This note proposes no broader workflow policy and does not reopen the accepted reader rollout.","body":{"head":"b23c0263033b1d57e7a493d7c30b1ea6c53b980c","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:366d13eb85d890d8d3f9eaaafdea37f308de06a0, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8c84330c8616058098d5b153662e61a1a2ff71b2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02320b2eaa39a0ec7e47f31205c4b25afa46609f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0289268d00f17d2f7a127faead22bc78ee18dd4c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03bf9ae04ffa1aadb0f8f5018e3936c2bb725